    static final String SCOPE="Original Monocle3 1.3.1 additive gene-wise models on complete caller-prepared raw-count or nonnegative normalized-expression populations. Original family/cleaning defaults may be selected explicitly. Preserve original offsets, Size_Factor estimation, model statuses, t/normal coefficient tests and grouped default-Holm q values. Optional native Hmisc-source Pearson filtering uses the supplied expression and score, with strict q/r thresholds, never coefficient-sign filtering. This is a standalone development component, not whole Monocle/Hmisc, study reproduction, recovered paper commits or biological certification.";
    static final String ACTION="Required action: inspect analysis-status.json and WARNINGS.md; require result_admitted=true before use. Retain full inputs, original source/models, RNG, process logs and failed/skipped attempts. Provide the exact separate Linux R4.3.3/Monocle3 1.3.1 profile and adjacent pinned jdistlib-all-0.10.2.jar. Install/download only where permitted. If required runtime/install/execution is unavailable or forbidden, SKIP3 skips dependent analysis. FAIL2 admits no partial batch: resolve the named integrity, input, scientific, original-model or capacity cause and retry NEW paths. Never switch families/editions, round normalized expression into counts, pool testing populations, drop failed genes/cells or replace NA/Inf to force success. Sparse Matrix Market coordinates must be unique; no duplicate summing/repair. Original non-OK model statuses remain failures even if coefficient values were returned. Portable audit modes test supplied statistics only and do not authenticate producers or repeat original model fitting.";
